---
title: Privacy policy
description: Which personal data nullish processes, why, where, and for how long.
---

This policy explains which personal data we process when you use nullish or visit this website, why, where and for how long.

## Applicable law

This privacy policy is designed to meet the requirements of the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP) and the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). However, whether and to what extent these laws are applicable depends on the individual case in question.

## What we process

Our policy is to collect personal data only for essential purposes and not to sell it to third parties.

**Identity and access**: we primarily process the personal data necessary for the operation and use of nullish. This includes your name, email address, and company affiliation, which are required for a functional login.

**Business data**: the business data you enter in nullish, such as clients, invoices, bank statements and journal entries, is hosted by our application. This data processing is necessary for you to use nullish as intended.

**AI assistant**: if you use the assistant, your requests and the data needed to answer them are processed by the AI model, hosted in Switzerland by Infomaniak.

**Payment processing**: to process card payments for nullish subscriptions, our billing partner, Stripe Payments Europe, Limited, processes personal data such as your name, email address, and the payment details you provide. Stripe may also collect identifying device data for the purpose of fraud detection in card payments.

**Correspondence**: we retain support requests and other correspondence, including your email address, so that we have the context of previous inquiries for reference when answering future questions.

**Technical logs**: we maintain technical logs. These help us identify issues and ensure security, for example by detecting suspicious activity. They contain information about account access and activity, and individual logs also collect the IP address of the access and details about the browser used.

**Website**: visit statistics for this website are collected without cookies, and the data is anonymized.

## Why

We primarily use the personal data we collect to conclude and process our contracts with our customers, particularly within the scope of nullish and its software-as-a-service services, as well as to comply with our legal obligations. If you work for such a customer, you may also be affected by this with your personal data in this role.

- To provide nullish and its features.
- To manage your subscription and billing.
- To send emails linked to your account, such as sign-in verification or a trial reminder.
- To keep nullish secure and fix problems.
- To meet our legal obligations, such as keeping our accounting records.

We don't sell your data, don't use it for advertising and don't use it to train AI models.

## Where and with whom

Your accounting data is stored and processed in Switzerland. We work with these providers:

| Provider                                           | Purpose             | Location                    |
| -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | --------------------------- |
| [Infomaniak](https://www.infomaniak.com)           | Server and AI model | Switzerland                 |
| [cloudscale](https://www.cloudscale.ch)            | Encrypted backups   | Switzerland                 |
| [Amazon Web Services](https://aws.amazon.com/ses/) | Sending emails      | Switzerland (Zurich region) |
| [Stripe](https://stripe.com)                       | Payments            | Ireland, United States      |

Stripe only receives what it needs to process payments.

If a recipient is located in a country without adequate legal data protection, we contractually oblige the recipient to comply with the applicable data protection standards (for this, we use the revised [standard contractual clauses](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/914/oj) of the European Commission), unless it is already subject to a legally recognised set of rules for ensuring data protection or we are able to rely on an exemption provision.

More details on the [Hosting](/en/data/) page.

## How long

We process and store your personal data for as long as it is necessary to fulfil our contractual and legal obligations or for the purposes otherwise pursued by the processing, i.e. for the duration of the entire business relationship and, beyond this, in accordance with statutory storage and documentation obligations. As soon as your personal data is no longer required for the above-mentioned purposes, it will generally be deleted or anonymised as far as possible. For operational data (e.g. system logs), generally shorter retention periods of twelve months or less apply.

- When an organization is deleted, its data is deleted for good 30 days later.
- Data may temporarily remain in infrastructure backups. It is also removed once the backup retention period expires and the backup is deleted.

## Security

We use technical and organisational security measures in accordance with recognised market standards to protect stored personal data against unintentional, unlawful or unauthorised manipulation, deletion, alteration, access, disclosure or use and against partial or complete loss. Our servers are located in Switzerland. The connection to our servers is encrypted with HTTPS. We regularly back up customer data, and the encrypted backups are stored in Switzerland with a separate provider. Our security measures are continuously adapted and improved in line with technological developments. We can't assume any guarantee for the security of data transmission on the Internet; in particular, there is a risk of access by third parties when data is transmitted by email.

## Cookies

nullish only uses the cookies needed to keep you signed in. There are no tracking or advertising cookies.

## Your rights

You have the following rights with regard to your personal data in accordance with the FADP (in particular, Art. 25 ff. FADP) or the GDPR (in particular, Arts. 12–23 GDPR). In principle, we also grant the rights contained in the GDPR to Swiss customers. However, we reserve the right to make a different assessment in individual cases.

- The right of access;
- The right to rectification;
- The right to erasure;
- The right to restriction of processing;
- The right to data portability;
- The right to object.

Please note, however, that we reserve the right to enforce the limitations imposed by law, such as when we are obliged to retain or process certain data, have an overriding interest in doing so (as far as we may invoke it), or require the data to assert claims.

The exercise of such rights usually requires that you clearly prove your identity. To assert your rights, you can contact us at [hi@nullish.ch](mailto:hi@nullish.ch).

For the data in your organizations, the organization is responsible. Requests from its clients or suppliers should go to it first, and we help it answer.

Each data subject also has the right to enforce their claims in court or to lodge a complaint with the competent data protection authority. The competent data protection authority in Switzerland is the Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner ([FDPIC](https://www.edoeb.admin.ch)).

## Changes

We may modify this privacy policy at any time without notice. The current version published on our website always applies. If the privacy policy forms part of an agreement with you, we will notify you in the event of an update by email, via your nullish account, or by other appropriate means.

## Controller

The party responsible for this privacy policy is Fluster GmbH, c/o The Hub Zürich Association, Sihlquai 131, 8005 Zürich.
